messages.text:
{#select place}{#case house}The kitchen smells of bread and woodsmoke. Aunt Odile's cat watches you from the warm end of the table.{#case square}The square is a cobbled bowl of noise: carts, pigeons, shouted prices. A lamp-post carries a half-peeled poster for the Trials.{#case market}Awnings in every colour lean over the stalls. A fishmonger and a cheese seller are halfway through a feud that has outlived both their fathers.{#case forge}Heat rolls out of the open doors. Mara Voss does not look up from the glowing bar on her anvil.{#case archive}Dust lies in the slats of light. Archivist Pell sits among towers of ledgers like a king of a very quiet country.{#case tavern}The Gilded Heron is half full and wholly loud. Someone is tuning a fiddle with more hope than skill.{#case docks}Gulls argue over a crate of herring. Beyond the last pier, a broken bridge stands over the river like a sentence that lost its end.{#case quarry}White stone climbs on every side. Your footsteps ring back from the cut walls.{#case green}Bunting snaps in the wind. The Festival Green is a ring of lanterns, trestle tables and nervous people.{#default}Hollowbrook.{/select}
{#if query evening()}The light has gone long and gold.{#else}The day is still young enough to spend.{/if}
{#if query nearly_solved()}You have the feeling of a puzzle that is nearly solved.{/if}
